---
source: crates/broza-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(args)
---
Read and write configuration keys

Usage: broza config [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  get    Print the value of one key
  set    Validate a value and write it to the configuration file
  list   Print every key with its effective value
  path   Print the path of the configuration file in use
  reset  Restore one key, or every key, to its default

Options:
      --json            JSON output on stdout. Disables color, progress and interactivity
      --csv             Flat CSV output on stdout. Only on tabular commands
  -o, --output <FILE>   Write output to a file instead of stdout
      --no-color        Disable ANSI color. Automatic without a TTY or with `NO_COLOR` set
  -q, --quiet           Errors only. Silences progress and non-critical warnings
  -v, --verbose...      More diagnostic detail on stderr. Repeatable
      --config <FILE>   Alternative configuration file [default: ~/.config/broza/config.toml]
      --profile <NAME>  Configuration profile to apply
      --no-cache        Ignore the scan cache and force a full analysis
  -h, --help            Print help
